{
  "swagger": "2.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "dynamo/mcs/v1/common.proto",
    "description": "The Multi-Cluster Services (KEP-1645) registry API of the Dynamo Global\nRouter.\n\nThe API is additive only; a breaking change means a new v2 package. Every\nRPC is served over gRPC and mirrored as REST/JSON through the\ngoogle.api.http annotations. JSON follows the proto3 JSON mapping\n(lowerCamelCase field names, enums as strings, 64-bit integers as strings).\nServer streams are rendered as newline-delimited JSON objects of the form\n{\"result\": {...}}.\n\nErrors are google.rpc.Status values carrying a google.rpc.ErrorInfo with\ndomain \"mcs.dynamo.nvidia.com\" and one of these reasons:\n\n  STALE_GENERATION        FAILED_PRECONDITION. The write carried a\n                          generation that does not exceed the stored one.\n                          ErrorInfo.metadata[\"current_generation\"] holds the\n                          stored generation; a PreconditionFailure detail\n                          repeats it.\n  LEASE_EPOCH_MISMATCH    ABORTED. A heartbeat carried an epoch other than\n                          the current lease epoch. Register again.\n  CLUSTER_NOT_REGISTERED  FAILED_PRECONDITION or NOT_FOUND. The cluster has\n                          no registration in the clusterset.\n  TOO_MANY_ENDPOINTS      INVALID_ARGUMENT. An endpoint set exceeds 1000\n                          endpoints.\n  TOO_MANY_WATCHERS       RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED. The replica serves\n                          --max-watchers streams already.\n  STORE_UNAVAILABLE       UNAVAILABLE. The backing store did not answer.\n                          Retry with backoff.\n  SHUTTING_DOWN           UNAVAILABLE. The replica is draining. Reconnect;\n                          another replica serves the request.\n\nInvalid input is INVALID_ARGUMENT with a google.rpc.BadRequest detail.\n\nLimits: identifiers (clusterset, cluster, namespace, name) are DNS-1123\nlabels; 64 labels; 32 annotations totalling at most 16 KiB; 64 ports; 1000\nendpoints per export per cluster; 16 attributes per endpoint; 4 MiB per\nmessage.",
    "version": "version not set"
  },
  "tags": [
    {
      "name": "ClusterService"
    },
    {
      "name": "ServiceExportService"
    },
    {
      "name": "ServiceImportService"
    },
    {
      "name": "ServerInfoService"
    }
  ],
  "consumes": [
    "application/json"
  ],
  "produces": [
    "application/json"
  ],
