    "v1EventType": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "EVENT_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED",
        "EVENT_TYPE_SNAPSHOT_START",
        "EVENT_TYPE_UPSERT",
        "EVENT_TYPE_DELETE",
        "EVENT_TYPE_SNAPSHOT_END",
        "EVENT_TYPE_BOOKMARK"
      ],
      "default": "EVENT_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED",
      "description": "EventType is the kind of a watch event.\n\nA watch sends SNAPSHOT_START, one UPSERT per object, SNAPSHOT_END with the\nrevision, then UPSERT and DELETE deltas, and a BOOKMARK every 5 s. A watch\nopened with a usable resume_revision skips the snapshot and receives only\nthe deltas after that revision; an unknown or stale revision yields a new\nsnapshot, never an error. A slow watcher is re-snapshotted, not\ndisconnected.\n\n - EVENT_TYPE_SNAPSHOT_START: Start of a full snapshot. Clients discard their local state.\n - EVENT_TYPE_UPSERT: The object was created or changed; it carries the full object.\n - EVENT_TYPE_DELETE: The object was removed; it carries the last known object.\n - EVENT_TYPE_SNAPSHOT_END: End of a full snapshot; revision is set.\n - EVENT_TYPE_BOOKMARK: Keepalive carrying the current revision; no object."
    },
